<title>USA: Texas trims prorated natgas field allowables.</title>
<headline>Texas trims prorated natgas field allowables.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Texas Railroad Commission on Monday said December allowable natural gas production from prorated fields in the state was set at 71.5 billion cubic feet (bcf).</p>
<p>The allowable production was down 5.9 bcf from actual production of 77.4 bcf in December 1995, the commission said. The decline primarily reflects wells pulled out of the prorated production system.</p>
<p>The commission estimated natural gas in storage in November at 222.3 bcf. Gas in storage for October 1996 was about 226.2 bcf compared to 286.1 bcf in October 1995.</p>
</text>
